      "title": "Opt2Skill: Imitating Dynamically-Feasible Whole-Body Trajectories for Versatile Humanoid Loco-Manipulation",
      "takeaway": "Opt2Skill is an end-to-end pipeline that combines model-based trajectory optimization with reinforcement learning to achieve robust whole-body loco-manipulation for the Digit humanoid robot. It uses differential dynamic programming (DDP) to generate dynamically feasible and contact-consistent reference motions, then trains RL policies to track these optimal trajectories. The paper reports that Opt2Skill outperforms baselines using human demonstrations and inverse kinematics-based references in motion tracking and task success rates, and that incorporating torque information improves contact force tracking in tasks like wiping a table. The approach was transferred to real-world applications. While reading, inspect how the DDP-generated trajectories are encoded as RL rewards and how torque information is integrated to improve contact force tracking.",
